        <mxCell id="blk" value="Deploy blockers — from the project's own review corpus (review/findings.json: 198 findings, 65 open, 22 carried)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#b85450;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=12;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="690" width="1460" height="400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="blk1" value="&lt;b&gt;5 FATAL findings still open or carried&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;X-001 — CLOSED: acl/access parse, bind, and execute; visibility matrix green&lt;br&gt;X-003 — no performance numbers, no executed restore/DR evidence&lt;br&gt;X-084 — no runnable end-to-end product despite broad platform claims&lt;br&gt;Y-005 — grant manifest is not an authority-complete semantic contract&lt;br&gt;AA-007 — deployment-scoped space creation unrepresentable in current types" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="730" width="460" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="blk2" value="&lt;b&gt;24 CRITICAL findings open or partial&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Clustered in four areas:&lt;br&gt;· &lt;b&gt;Atomicity&lt;/b&gt; — AA-004 CLOSED: domain write and command append share one transaction with row locks; replay completion (AA-005) owed&lt;br&gt;· &lt;b&gt;Fencing&lt;/b&gt; — stale replay-lease holders can mutate successor state (AA-005, C4-005, SH4-002)&lt;br&gt;· &lt;b&gt;Crypto&lt;/b&gt; — blind-index rotation, SealedRef enforcement, genesis import bypass (AA-013, AA-023, AA-024)&lt;br&gt;· &lt;b&gt;Ordering&lt;/b&gt; — cursor stability and multi-source total order (X-059, AA-017, M4-008)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fde8e6;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="570" y="730" width="460" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="blk3" value="&lt;b&gt;Operational readiness — barely started&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;· ~60 commits on main, CI green&lt;br&gt;· no .github/ — no CI, no test gate&lt;br&gt;· no Dockerfile, compose, terraform, helm, or migrations&lt;br&gt;· &lt;b&gt;pooled tokio-postgres in ordo-exec&lt;/b&gt; — the conformance harness shells out to psql by choice&lt;br&gt;· no backup/restore or DR drill has been executed (X-072)&lt;br&gt;· no published performance numbers of any kind" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fde8e6;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="730" width="440" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="blk4" value="&lt;b&gt;Verdict: still not deployable — but the compiler is no longer a stub.&lt;/b&gt;   Source text now reaches PostgreSQL and comes back with the rows the corpus says it must: schema graph → binder → planner → seeded execution, on 7 cases. What that does NOT change: authorization (X-001) is untouched, the executor, CLI, cost gate and guard cases all run; artifact registration remains. The next milestone is the `unbounded` cost gate and `ordo check`/`ordo plan` — a compiler nobody can invoke is not a deploy path." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=14;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="80" y="950" width="1420" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
